WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.150
Over the holidays, our garden

2
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:04.150
sensor said the soil was fine.

3
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.360
Every day, the same number: forty percent.

4
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:10.920
We came back to dead seedlings.

5
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:14.260
The battery had died on day three, and

6
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.220
the screen kept its last reading.

7
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.170
Today: keep a sensor project running

8
00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:23.050
and secure, long after launch day.

9
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.280
Every sensor system needs upkeep,

10
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.240
so plan it before launch.

11
00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:30.710
Change batteries on a schedule.

12
00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.150
Clean off dust, mud and leaves,

13
00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:35.830
which give false readings.

14
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:38.970
And check against a trusted sensor

15
00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:41.490
each term, because sensors drift.

16
00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.620
Now the silent failure.

17
00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.850
A heartbeat is a short message a

18
00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.030
device sends on a schedule, even

19
00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:51.170
when nothing has changed.

20
00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.700
If the heartbeats stop, the

21
00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:54.900
system warns someone.

22
00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.680
No heartbeat for two hours?

23
00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.030
Check the battery, the

24
00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.610
wires and the signal.

25
00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.110
Show when each reading

26
00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:05.990
arrived, not just the number.

27
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:08.870
Forty percent, last seen three

28
00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:10.690
days ago, tells the truth.

29
00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.820
Forty percent on its own

30
00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.160
hides the problem.

31
00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:15.850
Quick check!

32
00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:18.990
Our dashboard says the tank is half full,

33
00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.050
and it has said so for four days.

34
00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.090
What should we check first?

35
00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.020
Check when the last reading came.

36
00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.450
A school tank is used every day, so a

37
00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:31.550
number that never moves is suspicious.

38
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.830
A heartbeat and a last-seen time

39
00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.430
would have warned you on day one.

40
00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.370
Now security.

41
00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.380
In twenty sixteen, the Mirai

42
00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:43.200
malware took over hundreds of

43
00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.060
thousands of cameras and routers.

44
00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.580
It simply tried a list of about

45
00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.220
sixty factory passwords.

46
00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.200
Then it used those devices to

47
00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.000
knock major websites offline.

48
00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.880
So, four habits from day one.

49
00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.760
Change every default password.

50
00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.050
Install updates for the

51
00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:04.470
devices and the router.

52
00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:07.350
Put sensors on their own network,

53
00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:09.050
apart from school records.

54
00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:12.090
And collect only the data you need.

55
00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.900
Projects often die when

56
00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:15.780
their champion leaves.

57
00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:20.120
So hand over early: a one-page guide by

58
00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.420
the device, and the passwords kept by

59
00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.000
the school, not on your phone.

60
00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:26.710
Train two people, not one.

61
00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:28.890
Each year, older pupils

62
00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.330
train the next class.

63
00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:32.210
Your turn.

64
00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.180
The project teacher is moving schools.

65
00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:39.350
The sensors work well, and only

66
00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:40.770
she knows the passwords.

67
00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:43.730
Will the system keep running?

68
00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:47.840
Not for long: with no guide and one

69
00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.580
person, the first flat battery ends it.

70
00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.200
Remember: upkeep on a rota, a heartbeat

71
00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.240
for silent failures, four security habits,

72
00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.820
and a handover before anyone leaves.

73
00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.710
Try it in class tomorrow: a failure hunt.

74
00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.210
Pupils list what could stop your

75
00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:11.010
sensor: a flat battery, mud, theft, a

76
00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:13.050
lost password, the holidays.

77
00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.260
For each: how would you

78
00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.140
notice, and who fixes it?

79
00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:20.190
Next time: using the data fairly.
